
This is a list of example scenrarios that I wish to create. I can then make unit tests to see how they work.
Rules: Must only be a single roll at per action (too confusing otherwise).
Rules: All items are single use.

I punch the goblin.
-> Success, the goblin takes 1 wound.
-> Med Success, the goblin is stunned.
-> Failure, player gains stress.

I punch the goblin, but it's spiky
-> Success, the goblin takes 1 wound. (player gain 1 wound)
-> Med Success, the goblin is stunned. (player gain 1 wound)
-> Failure, target gains stress.

I throw the table at the goblin
-> Success, the table shatters and the goblin takes 1 wound.
-> Med Success, the goblin is stunned.
-> Failure, player gains stress.

I throw the table at the goblin, but player is blinded.
-> Success, the table shatters but ther'es only a 50% chance the gobin takes 1 wound.
-> Med Success, the goblin takes 1 wound.
-> Failure, player gains stress.

I throw the table at the goblin, and the goblin is suprised / stunned.
-> Success, the table shatters and the goblin takes 2 wounds.
-> Med Success, the goblin takes 1 wound.
-> Failure, player gains stress.

